    "body": "#### vim-patch:9.2.1149: crash when reading a truncated spell file\n\nProblem:  read_tree_node() does not check for a negative return\n          value from getc() causing a crash. (Yuyao Jiang)\nSolution: Reject a negative values.\n\nrelated: vim/vim#21373\n\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/366777aedf950a099685086a22e09489884189c7\n\nCo-authored-by: Christian Brabandt <cb@256bit.org>\n\n\n#### vim-patch:9.2.1154: tests: invalid 'B' flag passed to writefile()\n\nProblem:  Tests pass an invalid 'B' flag to writefile()\n          (after v9.2.1149).\nSolution: Remove the flag (zeertzjq).\n\ncloses: vim/vim#21408\n\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/d8249e23d9b31cd859482102e06ad19a56db00df",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-01T08:03:55Z",
